    "Invasive approaches for patients with NSTE-ACS lead to improved outcomes and are recommended for those at a high risk of death or MI. The GRACE score is used to determine risk levels. For those with ongoing ischemia or hemodynamic compromise, individualized treatment is advised. High-risk patients benefit most from invasive procedures, which are especially effective in reducing mortality and recurrent events. Immediate revascularization may not significantly alter outcomes compared to strategic planning, but quick interventions can aid patients with ST segment elevation myocardial infarction. Trials like SHOCK and TIMACS support strategic angiography timing based on patient condition and risk scores.": [],
